August 29th, 1774

The saloon’s been quieter than usual since Bart took over as sheriff. Folks still give him the side eye, 
but they’re starting to come around. Hell, even old Olsen tipped his hat this morning. Progress is slow,
but it’s progress nonetheless.

Taggart was spotted on the outskirts near Dead Man’s Gulch. Likely scouting. I don’t like it. That 
buffoon’s never had an original thought in his life, but someone’s clearly feeding him instructions.

Bart thinks Hedley’s planning something bigger than just scaring folks off. Maybe it’s the land, 
maybe it’s the railroads. Whatever it is, I’ll keep my piece loaded and my bottle half full.

Mongo wandered into the sheriff’s office today. Didn’t say a word. Just sat in the corner and stared 
at the wall. After an hour, he grunted, stood up, and walked out. Weird fella. Heart’s probably 
twice the size of mine.

- Jim “The Waco Kid”
